messages[14]{user,text}:
  user_1,[00:00] Hello? Hi Anita, it's Saanvi. I just got your email about the Critical‑Illness Rider.
  user_2,[00:04] Hi Saanvi! Yes, I sent that earlier today. Did you get a chance to look at it?
  user_1,[00:08] Umm... yeah, I skimmed through. The extra premium is about $45 per month, right? [typing]
  user_2,[00:12] That's correct. It would be added to your next premium due on 15 Nov 2026.
  user_1,[00:16] Great. So I want to go ahead and add the rider. Also, can we double‑check the beneficiary? I think it's still my husband, Rajesh.
  user_2,[00:20] Sure thing. Let me pull up your policy… [pause] …Yes, the current beneficiary is Rajesh Pillai, DOB 12/03/1978.
  user_1,[00:25] Perfect. No change needed there. And… uh, will the rider affect the sum assured?
  user_2,[00:30] Good question— the rider adds an additional cover of $50,000 on top of your base sum assured. Your overall coverage will be $250,000 now.
  user_1,[00:35] Got it. And the payment method stays the same? My auto‑debit from my checking account?
  user_2,[00:38] Yes, we’ll keep the same auto‑debit. I’ll just need your verbal consent to bind the rider.
  user_1,[00:42] I consent. Please go ahead.
  user_2,[00:45] All set! I’ve updated the system. You’ll see the rider reflected in your next statement and I’ll send a confirmation email shortly. Anything else I can help with?
  user_1,[00:50] No, that’s all. Thanks a lot!
  user_2,[00:52] You’re welcome! Have a great day, Saanvi.